From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Simon Elsbrock <simon@iodev.org>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 16:32:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm: dts: mediatek: add the Echo Dot (5th gen) (cannoli)
 device tree

The MT8519 SoC and the cannoli board device tree (ADR 0034), from Amazon's
5.4 release: mt8519.dtsi and mt8519-amzn.dtsi for the SoC, mt6395.dtsi for
the PMIC, cannoli-cheesecake.dtsi and cannoli-hvt.dts for the board, with the
MT8519 pinfunc, memory-port, EMI and the Amazon CPLD GPIO binding headers.
The tree compiles to cannoli-hvt.dtb on 6.12's dtc unchanged beyond the
binding headers it needs; nodes whose drivers are not yet ported are present
but inert until those land.

Built: mediatek/cannoli-hvt.dtb (ARCH=arm).
